// The dual of `namespaced_coexistence`: importing two same-short-named types WITHOUT aliases binds
// both to the same local name `Amount`, which is ambiguous — an E0020 collision. Aliasing (as in the
// coexistence fixture) is the way to admit both. The error points at the second, clashing import.
// expect: error E0020 at 8:13
// expect: exit 1
// (No `namespace`: the entry of package `App` derives `App.main` from its own file name.)
use App.Money.Amount;
use App.Geo.Amount;

a = Amount { cents: 1 };
echo a.cents;
